---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const partnership = [
  {
    title: 'Built to scale',
    body: 'Peak load is the design target: launches, press, seasonal demand, live events. The site holds when it matters, not just on a quiet Tuesday.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A team, not a ticket queue',
    body: 'A small senior team that knows your business and your stack. The people you talk to are the people who build.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Full-lifecycle management',
    body: 'Redesign is the starting point. Ongoing development, content operations, monitoring, security patching, and the operational side once the audit is done.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Security and compliance',
    body: 'End-of-life software, unpatched dependencies, missing consent management, accessibility gaps. Closed as part of the rebuild, not billed as extras.',
  },
];

const auditAreas = [
  {
    title: 'Storage & archive',
    body: 'Years of files in Drive or Dropbox, every one billed at active rates. We move the archive to object storage with a dashboard your team can search, and leave the working files where they are.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Software sprawl',
    body: 'Seats nobody uses, three tools doing one job, licenses renewing on autopilot. We inventory every subscription, tie it to a person and a purpose, and cut the dead weight.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Workflow',
    body: 'The hand-offs between tools are where the hours go. We trace how work actually moves through the company and replace the duct tape with something that runs on its own.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Enterprise | Griffith Creative"
  description="Griffith Creative designs, rebuilds, and manages high-traffic websites, and helps established companies build the systems they run on."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="min-h-[80vh] flex items-center">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 w-full">
      <p class="font-mono text-offwhite-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-8">
        Enterprise Partnerships
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem)] leading-[0.95] tracking-tight mb-10 max-w-6xl">
        Built for the companies<br />
        <span class="text-accent">that can't afford to go down.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-12">
        When traffic spikes, deadlines don't move, and stakeholders are watching, everything has to hold: the website, the storage, the tools your team runs on. We audit, rebuild, and manage the infrastructure established companies depend on, without enterprise bloat.
      </p>
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12" aria-label="Tracks">
        <li class="font-mono text-xs text-offwhite-muted border border-offwhite/15 rounded-full px-4 py-2">Web Partnerships</li>
        <li class="font-mono text-xs text-offwhite-muted border border-offwhite/15 rounded-full px-4 py-2">Systems</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-32">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-8 max-w-4xl">
        Most agencies weren't built for your traffic.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Your site isn't a brochure. It's a live product: generating leads, processing transactions, and representing your brand to every customer who finds you. A dated CMS, a stack of unmanaged tracking scripts, and a team that only shows up for the redesign isn't enough. You need infrastructure that scales on demand and a partner who's still there in month thirteen, not just week one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Total Cost of Ownership -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-offwhite-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">
            Total Cost of Ownership
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-6 text-balance">
            You're paying enterprise prices to keep old technology alive.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Legacy platforms accumulate cost the way they accumulate tech debt: enterprise hosting contracts, redundant CDN layers, extended support for end-of-life software, licenses for services you stopped using years ago, and a retainer just to keep it all standing. We audit what you're paying for, then rebuild on modern infrastructure that collapses most of that spend and outperforms what it replaces.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-6">
            <h3 class="text-offwhite text-lg mb-2">Audit the real cost</h3>
            <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
              We map every contract, license, and dependency in your current stack and show you what each one is for, and which ones are dead weight.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-6">
            <h3 class="text-offwhite text-lg mb-2">Rebuild on modern infrastructure</h3>
            <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Static-first architecture on a global edge network. Faster under load, more secure by default, and a fraction of the hosting bill.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-6">
            <h3 class="text-offwhite text-lg mb-2">Keep what works</h3>
            <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Your data relationships, your measurement stack, your content library. We migrate cleanly instead of burning it down.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Systems -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-offwhite-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">
        Systems
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-6 max-w-3xl text-balance">
        Systems that work the way you do.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-16">
        Most companies run on systems nobody chose. We sit with your team, learn how the work really happens, and rebuild the storage, software, and workflows around it. <a href="/systems" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4 hover:text-offwhite">More on Systems</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-x-12 gap-y-10">
        {auditAreas.map((item) => (
          <div class="border-t border-offwhite/15 pt-6">
            <h3 class="text-offwhite text-xl mb-3">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Partnership -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-offwhite-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-8">
        What Partnership Looks Like
      </p>

      <div class="divide-y divide-offwhite/15 border-t border-offwhite/15">
        {partnership.map((item) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,4fr)] gap-x-12 gap-y-2 py-7">
            <h3 class="text-offwhite text-xl">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-offwhite-muted leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Commitments -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-offwhite-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">
        What We Commit To
      </p>
      <p class="text-offwhite text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-snug tracking-tight max-w-4xl text-pretty">
        Uptime and performance monitoring on every site we manage. A response within one business day, usually much sooner. High-90s Lighthouse scores we measure before launch. Every saving from a systems rebuild checked against the invoices afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="border-t border-offwhite/10 py-32">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-6">
        Bring us the site, or the stack,<br />you can't afford to break.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-offwhite-muted text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
        The audit comes first: performance, structure, security, storage, software, and cost, mapped before you commit to anything. You'll know exactly what you're deciding on.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
